# Rootless Podman runtime

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — Read when the task router matches Compose
configuration, container workflow scripts, or the shared Podman adapter.

- Use unprivileged `podman` and `podman-compose`; never require Docker Desktop,
  Colima, `docker`, `docker compose`, `docker-compose`, `DOCKER_HOST`, or a
  Docker socket on this Linux workspace.
- Keep OCI-standard filenames such as `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`, and
  `docker-compose*.yaml`; filename compatibility does not select the runtime.
- Run committed workflows through `scripts/lib/podman_runtime.sh`. Production
  operators use project `hpcperfstats` (network `hpcperfstats_net`) and must
  **not** require `/data/user/$USER`. Tests use `hpcperfstats-test`; the
  long-running development stack uses `hpcperfstats-dev`. Teardown must stay
  project-scoped.
- Never run global image, build-cache, volume, network, container, or system
  prune on this shared server. `--keep-env` may preserve the selected project.
- For **test/dev only** (`HPCPERFSTATS_LOCAL_DATA_CONTRACT=1`): all non-DNF
  downloads, caches, tools, temporary files, image layers, writable layers, and
  volumes belong below `/data/user/$USER` or `/data/podman/$USER`. `/run/user/$UID`
  is allowed for required ephemeral rootless runtime state.
- `podman_runtime_require` always checks `podman` and `podman-compose` exist.
  For test/dev it must also fail closed unless Podman is rootless and its graph
  root, image store, volume path, cache, and temporary paths resolve below
  `/data`. Production project skips the `/data` layout and rootless storage
  checks so operator rebuilds do not invent `/data/user/root`.
- Rootless prerequisites (test/dev) include sufficiently large, non-overlapping
  `/etc/subuid` and `/etc/subgid` ranges for container uid 901860 and writable,
  correctly labeled `/data` storage. Do not fall back to rootful Podman for
  isolated test/dev stacks.

## Overlap

- `docker-compose-non-unit-testing.mdc` and
  `full-test-with-db-redis.mdc` define which committed workflow to run.
- `workspace-layout-and-python-env.mdc` defines the host Python environment.
